    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0353" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg321"/>

                <head>189. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Jordan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d189-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-07-17T20:36:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                                1958—8:36 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>159. Embtel 132.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d189-f2"/> Please inform Hussein in
                    response to his request for US military intervention that US immediately upon
                    receipt request consulted with UK at highest
                    level. UK has already responded by dispatch of
                    troops and US has indicated its full support for this <pb facs="0354" n="322"
                        xml:id="pg322"/> action by flying military planes over Jordan this morning
                    and statement of strong support issued today.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d189-f3"
                    /></p>
                <p>We trust these actions will give the necessary support to His Majesty in his
                    courageous and forthright efforts to maintain the independence and integrity of
                        HKJ. We will continue to keep the situation
                    under closest observation to determine whether further measures are
                    necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
